WEBVTT

1
00:00:17.184 --> 00:00:21.466
Jack groaned softly when he saw the swimmers gathered around the community pool.

2
00:00:22.486 --> 00:00:26.087
All the other guys on the team were wearing compression suits and goggles.

3
00:00:27.087 --> 00:00:29.388
He had on the swim trunks he'd worn yesterday.

4
00:00:30.268 --> 00:00:34.510
If only he had unpacked his things instead of falling asleep right after dinner!

5
00:00:35.651 --> 00:00:40.813
His mother had woken him early and lectured him about breaking his promise to unpack the night before.

6
00:00:41.794 --> 00:00:47.717
He'd searched for his goggles and compression suits, frantically digging through the moving boxes in his bedroom while

7
00:00:47.757 --> 00:00:52.439
the annoying Long-Hair Boys song played over and over on the other side of the wall.

8
00:01:00.248 --> 00:01:00.728
"Ooh, baby, baby, baby.

9
00:01:00.748 --> 00:01:01.268
Ooh, baby, baby, baby."

10
00:01:01.288 --> 00:01:03.970
The song had filled his head, but the search had come up empty.

11
00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:06.271
"Mommy, look!"

12
00:01:06.691 --> 00:01:07.351
Luke shouted.

13
00:01:07.951 --> 00:01:08.992
He was sitting with Mrs.

14
00:01:09.032 --> 00:01:11.873
Gibson on one of the lounge chairs arranged around the pool.

15
00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:17.155
A few other parents had come to the practice, but Luke was the only little kid here.

16
00:01:18.476 --> 00:01:21.337
Luke pointed at a huge guy on Jack's new team.

17
00:01:21.357 --> 00:01:23.478
"It's a superhero!"

18
00:01:24.998 --> 00:01:27.139
This time Jack groaned loudly.

19
00:01:28.916 --> 00:01:31.959
"I cannot believe Luke just said that," he thought.

20
00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:34.822
The huge guy walked over to Luke.

21
00:01:37.704 --> 00:01:43.030
He really was built like a superhero, tall, broad-shouldered, and muscular.

22
00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:44.971
"Hey, I'm Hulk."

23
00:01:46.112 --> 00:01:50.597
The name fit him like a glove—a gigantic glove.

24
00:01:50.617 --> 00:01:52.919
"Hello, I'm Luke."

25
00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:53.860
Luke grinned.

26
00:01:54.444 --> 00:02:00.069
"I'm four years old, and I like spaghetti and playing tag and sharing a bedroom with my big

27
00:02:00.089 --> 00:02:00.709
brother, Jack.

28
00:02:00.969 --> 00:02:01.910
He's right over there."

29
00:02:02.671 --> 00:02:03.832
Luke pointed at Jack.

30
00:02:05.733 --> 00:02:09.376
Hulk and most of Jack's new teammates looked Jack's way.

31
00:02:10.117 --> 00:02:11.918
Instantly Jack looked down.

32
00:02:11.938 --> 00:02:15.281
"My big brother is famous," Luke said.

33
00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:19.484
"He's the bestest swimmer in all of Small Rock, Oklahoma."

34
00:02:20.385 --> 00:02:21.066
Hulk laughed.

35
00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:26.781
So did most of the other kids.

36
00:02:30.064 --> 00:02:31.585
Jack's face grew hot.

37
00:02:31.605 --> 00:02:35.028
"This is so embarrassing," he thought.

38
00:02:36.269 --> 00:02:38.511
Luckily the coach was approaching the swimmers.

39
00:02:38.531 --> 00:02:42.454
"Listen up, Sharks!"

40
00:02:42.854 --> 00:02:43.935
Coach Shin bellowed.

41
00:02:44.556 --> 00:02:48.199
His deep voice seemed jarring compared with his short, slim body.

42
00:02:48.219 --> 00:02:54.264
"Our first meet of the summer is coming up quickly, and you all need a lot more practice.

43
00:02:55.148 --> 00:02:58.409
I'd like to introduce the new swimmer on our team, Jack Gibson."

44
00:02:59.769 --> 00:03:02.390
Jack raised his hand and smiled shyly.

45
00:03:04.371 --> 00:03:09.192
A boy standing nearby murmured, "The bestest swimmer in Tiny Pebble, Oklahoma."

46
00:03:10.012 --> 00:03:10.812
"He's famous!"

47
00:03:12.113 --> 00:03:13.433
a girl added, laughing.

48
00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:16.494
Jack dropped his hand as other kids grinned.

49
00:03:16.514 --> 00:03:19.655
"Time to work out," the coach said.

50
00:03:19.675 --> 00:03:23.896
"We'll do ten minutes of exercises on the grass before getting in the water."

51
00:03:24.956 --> 00:03:27.377
Everyone lined up in two long rows.

52
00:03:29.897 --> 00:03:31.398
Jack stood in the back row.

53
00:03:33.718 --> 00:03:35.839
He'd noticed Laura Perez in the first row.

54
00:03:36.919 --> 00:03:41.241
He would have been glad to see her here if his little brother hadn't just totally embarrassed him.

55
00:03:42.461 --> 00:03:48.263
The team did squat thrusts, push-ups, and a bunch of other exercises that Jack had never done before.

56
00:03:51.203 --> 00:03:53.384
The ten minutes seemed to last an hour.

57
00:03:55.124 --> 00:03:57.005
"Everyone in the water for vertical jumps!"

58
00:03:57.366 --> 00:03:58.306
Coach Shin barked.

59
00:03:58.326 --> 00:04:00.688
"Keep your arms straight up in the air.

60
00:04:00.988 --> 00:04:02.609
Hulk, you'll be in front, leading.

61
00:04:03.129 --> 00:04:04.450
Everyone, keep up the pace."

62
00:04:05.531 --> 00:04:08.633
Jack followed his new teammates to the shallow end of the pool.

63
00:04:11.475 --> 00:04:13.956
Hulk started quickly and didn't let up.

64
00:04:14.897 --> 00:04:19.120
Jump and land, jump and land, jump and land.

65
00:04:23.436 --> 00:04:29.181
Jack had done this drill in Oklahoma, but the pace was much faster here, and Jack's swimming trunks

66
00:04:29.301 --> 00:04:29.981
weighed him down.

67
00:04:30.942 --> 00:04:33.644
Jack spotted his mom leading Luke toward the gate.

68
00:04:36.406 --> 00:04:40.810
She'd told Jack that she was going to do some errands this morning and she'd be back after

69
00:04:40.870 --> 00:04:43.432
practice. "Bye, Jack!"

70
00:04:43.772 --> 00:04:45.314
Luke screamed, waving to him.

71
00:04:47.275 --> 00:04:48.536
Jack quickly looked away.

72
00:04:49.197 --> 00:04:53.180
He jumped and landed, jumped and landed, jumped and landed.

73
00:04:57.618 --> 00:05:00.020
He was so tired he could hardly think straight.

74
00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:05.363
He jumped and landed, jumped and landed, jumped and— "Ha-ha!"

75
00:05:05.843 --> 00:05:10.445
Jack suddenly realized that the kids closest to him were laughing at something.

76
00:05:10.465 --> 00:05:12.787
"Uh-oh," he thought.

77
00:05:12.807 --> 00:05:14.188
"What's so funny?"

78
00:05:14.208 --> 00:05:18.410
"Do you always hum Long-Hair Boys songs at swim practice?"

79
00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:19.931
the guy next to him asked.

80
00:05:21.011 --> 00:05:21.852
Jack grimaced.

81
00:05:22.464 --> 00:05:27.888
That dumb song had played so many times through his bedroom wall, it had implanted itself in his

82
00:05:27.968 --> 00:05:29.229
brain like a parasite!

83
00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:32.632
"Nope!" Jack tried to make a joke.

84
00:05:32.652 --> 00:05:36.094
"Ha-ha! It must be the stress of the move."

85
00:05:37.095 --> 00:05:40.918
Jump and land, jump and land, jump and land.

86
00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:49.584
Jack wished he could jump high in the air and land right back in Oklahoma.

87
00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:55.301
By the time Coach Shin announced it was time for the team to work on their swim strokes,

88
00:05:56.081 --> 00:05:58.002
Jack was ready to go back to bed.

89
00:05:58.882 --> 00:05:59.962
His arms ached.

90
00:06:00.603 --> 00:06:01.583
His legs ached.

91
00:06:02.463 --> 00:06:03.403
His head ached.

92
00:06:04.164 --> 00:06:06.584
Even his face ached from grimacing so much.

93
00:06:07.685 --> 00:06:09.085
"Jack," the coach said.

94
00:06:09.105 --> 00:06:10.705
"Do you know all the strokes?"

95
00:06:12.106 --> 00:06:12.746
Jack nodded.

96
00:06:13.246 --> 00:06:13.926
Of course he did.

97
00:06:14.586 --> 00:06:16.447
He'd taken years of swimming lessons.

98
00:06:17.027 --> 00:06:19.988
And he'd been on Small Rock's swim team since he was eight years old.

99
00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:22.541
"Do you have a specialty?

100
00:06:23.061 --> 00:06:24.903
Something to help the team at the upcoming meet?

101
00:06:25.584 --> 00:06:27.465
We'll be swimming against our biggest rival."

102
00:06:27.485 --> 00:06:30.368
"I'm good at breaststroke," Jack said.

103
00:06:30.388 --> 00:06:32.950
"Let's see what you've got," the coach said.

104
00:06:32.970 --> 00:06:35.432
"Now?" Jack asked.

105
00:06:35.452 --> 00:06:40.217
"No. At midnight," a kid named Sebastien said sarcastically.

106
00:06:41.017 --> 00:06:41.918
More laughter.

107
00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:48.364
Jack hurried to the edge of the pool, dived in, and swam two laps.

108
00:06:53.652 --> 00:06:58.473
His heavy swim trunks slowed him down, and he wasn't used to racing without goggles.

109
00:06:59.794 --> 00:07:02.034
Plus, the warm-up had drained his energy.

110
00:07:02.614 --> 00:07:05.975
He wasn't terrible, but he knew he could swim much faster.

111
00:07:05.995 --> 00:07:10.437
"Good," his new coach said when Jack got out of the pool.

112
00:07:12.177 --> 00:07:14.398
But there was no enthusiasm in his voice.

113
00:07:14.418 --> 00:07:17.478
"Let me try one more time," Jack said.

114
00:07:18.119 --> 00:07:20.939
Before the coach could say no, Jack dived in again.

115
00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:26.562
But in his rush, he did a belly flop, his stomach loudly slapping the water.

116
00:07:29.224 --> 00:07:31.886
He could immediately hear some other swimmers laughing.

117
00:07:34.968 --> 00:07:38.931
It took a few seconds for Jack to find his rhythm and do the breaststroke across the pool.

118
00:07:42.133 --> 00:07:44.574
He knew he'd swum even slower than before.

119
00:07:45.815 --> 00:07:51.039
As he walked back toward the group, he heard a girl mutter, "If that dude is the best

120
00:07:51.199 --> 00:07:55.574
on his team in Pebbletown, his team must be really bad."

121
00:07:57.436 --> 00:07:58.417
Sebastien laughed.

122
00:07:59.918 --> 00:08:03.340
"I think he's from Small Rock, not Pebbletown."

123
00:08:04.281 --> 00:08:06.183
That was the last straw.

124
00:08:06.203 --> 00:08:08.465
"I'm out of here," Jack thought.

125
00:08:09.345 --> 00:08:11.827
When practice was over, he went over to the coach.

126
00:08:11.847 --> 00:08:15.991
"I don't think I'm right for this team.

127
00:08:16.551 --> 00:08:16.951
I quit.

128
00:08:17.612 --> 00:08:20.394
Good-bye." The coach blinked in surprise.

129
00:08:20.414 --> 00:08:22.376
"You've only been to one practice."

130
00:08:23.276 --> 00:08:24.338
"Thanks for giving me a chance."

131
00:08:24.978 --> 00:08:27.682
Jack grabbed his towel and hurried from the pool.
